  "Question": "The Fort Worth Zoo has a number of two-legged birds and a number of four-legged mammals. On one visit to the zoo, Margie counted \\(200\\) heads and \\(522\\) legs. How many of the animals that Margie counted were two-legged birds?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 61 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 122 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 139 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 150 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 161 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The \\(200\\) heads mean there are \\(200\\) animals. If all were birds, they would have \\(200\\cdot2=400\\) legs.\n\nReplacing one imagined bird with a mammal keeps the animal count unchanged and adds \\(4-2=2\\) legs. The actual count has \\(522-400=122\\) extra legs, so there must be\n\\[\n122\\div2=61\n\\]\nmammals. The remaining \\(200-61=139\\) animals are birds. Indeed, \\(2\\cdot139+4\\cdot61=522\\), as required. There are \\(\\boxed{139}\\) birds, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
